      "id": "q-1779993358184-78787",
      "order": 1,
      "question": "What is the acute angle between the lines whose slopes are $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $3$?",
      "type": "mcq",
      "options": [
        {
          "letter": "A",
          "text": "$30^\\circ$",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "index": 0,
          "imageUrl": "",
          "explanation": "Incorrect. The calculation yields $\\tan \\theta = 1$, which corresponds to $45^\\circ$."
        },
        {
          "letter": "B",
          "text": "$45^\\circ$",
          "isCorrect": true,
          "index": 1,
          "imageUrl": "",
          "explanation": "Correct. The calculation confirms $\\tan \\theta = 1$, so $\\theta = 45^\\circ$."
        },
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "text": "$60^\\circ$",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "index": 2,
          "imageUrl": "",
          "explanation": "Incorrect. The calculation does not support this angle."
        },
        {
          "letter": "D",
          "text": "$90^\\circ$",
          "isCorrect": false,
          "index": 3,
          "imageUrl": "",
          "explanation": "Incorrect. The lines are not perpendicular."
        }
      ],
      "answer": "",
      "alternateAnswers": [],
      "explanation": "Let $m_1 = \\frac{1}{2}$ and $m_2 = 3$. The formula for the angle $\\theta$ between two lines is $\\tan \\theta = \\left| \\frac{m_2 - m_1}{1 + m_1 m_2} \\right|$. Substituting the values, $\\tan \\theta = \\left| \\frac{3 - \\frac{1}{2}}{1 + \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 3} \\right| = \\left| \\frac{\\frac{5}{2}}{\\frac{5}{2}} \\right| = 1$. Since $\\tan \\theta = 1$, the acute angle $\\theta = 45^\\circ$.",
      "hint": "Use the formula for the angle between two lines: $\\tan \\theta = \\left| \\frac{m_2 - m_1}{1 + m_1 m_2} \\right|$.",
      "marks": 4,
      "negativeMark": 0,
      "negativeMarking": false,
      "imageUrl": "",
      "subject": "calculus",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "hasError": false
    },
